* First watch (22:57)  By the way shaped: 48 35 n 5 30 w passed abeam; the course shaped for 48 15 n 5 05 w.
  First watch (22:57)  Shaped a course for 48° 15' N, 5° 05' W: ESE by account, 61 miles. Allowing the ebb, a knot and a half to the SW, steer E by S to make it good; the allowance holds till the tide turns, about a quarter past one in the middle watch. E by S (105°) lies across the wind from her head, by the stern; she is worn round for it. Stations for wearing ship.
